This confirms the persistence gap.
Right now runtimeProjectToProject() only creates an in-memory Project object:
TypeScriptreturn runtimeProjectToProject(runtimeProject);
It does not write it into:
TypeScriptprojectRepository
So runtime projects appear in the dashboard because storedProjects is set from runtime discovery, but lumina.projects.all stays empty.
Production fix: when a runtime project is discovered and no local record exists, create a durable repository record once, then use that saved project.
Safe patch:
Bashcat > /tmp/patch.py <<'PY'
from pathlib import Path

path = Path(
    "apps/lumina-builder/src/context/WorkspaceContext.tsx"
)

text = path.read_text()

old = """            if (localProject) {
              return {
                ...localProject,
                runtime: "warm",
              } as Project;
            }

            return runtimeProjectToProject(runtimeProject);
          });"""

new = """            if (localProject) {
              return {
                ...localProject,
                runtime: "warm",
              } as Project;
            }

            const discoveredProject =
              runtimeProjectToProject(
                runtimeProject,
              );

            projectRepository.create(
              discoveredProject,
              undefined,
            );

            return discoveredProject;
          });"""

if old not in text:
    raise SystemExit(
        "Runtime project mapping block not found"
    )

path.write_text(
    text.replace(old, new, 1)
)

print(
    "Runtime-discovered projects now persist to projectRepository"
)
PY

python3 /tmp/patch.py

npm run build
After green, verify in browser console after reload:
JavaScriptJSON.parse(
  localStorage.getItem("lumina.projects.all") ??
  "[]"
).map(p => p.id)
Expected:
JavaScript[
  "acmo-atlas",
  "elegance-sync-app",
  "group-home-harmony",
  "ride-craft-ai"
]
